      "text": "The Windows Subsystem Linux will mount the C: drive as /mnt/c.  By default the file permissions will be read/write/executable for all, this is bad because to use ssh-keys stricter permissions are required. To solve this create the /etc/wsl.conf file with the following content and restart the shell.\n\n[automount] enable=true root=/mnt options=\"metadata\"",
